# MovieFlix Landing Page

Static landing page for **MovieFlix**, a movie tracker Android app. Currently **hero section only** — user directs what to add next; do not expand scope unless asked.

## Stack & Files

- **HTML/CSS only** — no JS, no framework, no build step
- `index.html` — hero markup
- `styles.css` — all styles
- `asset/refernce.png` — **design reference** (match this)
- `asset/mock_up_2.png` — phone + rock mockup (PNG includes rock; it occludes the glow)

## Hero Markup

```html
<div class="hero__blue-glow">
  <span class="hero__glow-layer hero__glow-layer--outer"></span>
  <span class="hero__glow-layer hero__glow-layer--mid"></span>
  <span class="hero__glow-layer hero__glow-layer--core"></span>
</div>
<h1 class="hero__title">MOVIEFLIX</h1>
<img class="hero__mockup" src="asset/mock_up_2.png" />
```

## Hero Layout (z-index)

| Layer | Element | z-index |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Vignette | `.hero::after` | 0 |
| Glow | `.hero__blue-glow` + 3 child layers | 1 |
| Title | `.hero__title` | 2 |
| Mockup | `.hero__mockup` | 3 |

## Design Direction

- Dark cinematic background (`--black: #02030a`)
- Large glowing **MOVIEFLIX** title (Inter 900, white text-shadow bloom)
- Phone mockup on rock at bottom center
- Blue backlight **emerging from behind the rock** — not a phone-shaped halo
- Directional lighting: **heavily biased to the right shoulder** of the phone/rock under "FLIX"

## Reference Glow (`asset/refernce.png`)

The reference glow is **free-flow** (organic, right-biased backlight) and reads as **3 distinct blue layers**:

1. **Core** — tiny white / ice-blue hotspot at phone–rock junction (light source, right-biased at ~56%)
2. **Mid** — saturated electric blue plume rising upward-right behind phone under "FLIX"
3. **Outer** — deep navy, large soft feather, fades slowly to black; spreads wider on the right

Light hugs the rock surface and spills sideways along the rock top. Top of frame stays pure black.

## Glow Implementation

**Container** `.hero__blue-glow`:
- `bottom: clamp(15px, 4vh, 60px)` — positioned lower behind the rock base
- `width: min(62vw, 780px)`, `height: min(42vw, 470px)` — balanced medium footprint framing the rock
- `transform: translateX(-50%)` with `left: 50%` (centered)

**Layers** (each independent blur + gradient; `display: block` on spans):

| Class | Blur | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| `--core` | 16px | White → ice-blue hotspot centered at rock/phone rim (`44% × 44%`, `bottom: 10%`) |
| `--mid` | 42px | Electric blue with exponential decay curve (`inset: -14% -22%`), no box edges |
| `--outer` | 68px | Atmospheric navy fog (`inset: -35% -45%`), soft 7-stop falloff |

Gradient anchors use exponential / inverse-square falloff curves so the glow seamlessly feathers into black with zero visible contour edges.

## Do

- Keep 3 layers separate — merging into one gradient looks flat/uniform
- Tune position against `asset/refernce.png` (mainly `bottom` clamp + layer opacities)
- Keep `.hero` as `overflow: visible` so `filter: blur()` is not clipped
- Use `overflow-x: hidden` on `body` only
- Black `drop-shadow` on mockup for depth only

## Do Not

- Blue `drop-shadow` on `.hero__mockup` (creates phone-shaped glow)
- `overflow: hidden` on `.hero` (clips blurred glow)
- Aggressive `mask-image` on glow (hard clipped edges)
- Flat short container (e.g. 28vw height) — glow disappears behind rock
- Push glow off-screen with large `translateY`
- Pin all gradient energy at container bottom edge (100%) — stays hidden behind mockup

